# G121 — YouTube Downloader

*v2. See `youtube-downloader.md` for prose: concurrency as slot count,
resumable bytes-done, exponential backoff as pure function, format-policy
as data value, 5-state FSM with bounded self-loop.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Offline Archive

[offline-archive @videos
    IN ORDER TO
        download tagged videos within a bandwidth budget
        respecting retry policy on transient failures
        while preserving progress across retries

    @mgr <- [ytd[new-manager {max-concurrent: 3,
                               bandwidth-bps: 50000000,
                               retry-policy: {max-attempts: 3,
                                               initial-ms: 1000,
                                               multiplier: 2}}]]

    for @video in @videos
        @format <- [ytd[pick-format {formats: @video:formats,
                                       policy: {kind: "best-under",
                                                 cap-bytes: 500000000}}]]
        @format || -> #warn "no format under 500MB for " + @video:title
        [ytd[enqueue {manager: @mgr,
                       video-id: @video:id, format: @format}]]

    until @all-done [
        at @every 100 ms
            [ytd[tick {manager: @mgr, ms: 100}]]
            #progress
                active: @mgr:active-count
                pending: @mgr:pending-queue count
                downloads: @mgr:downloads

        sync @network-errors (@download-id)
            -> [ytd[report-failure {manager: @mgr, id: @download-id}]]
    ]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[ytd
    new-manager                 {max-concurrent, bandwidth-bps, retry-policy}
    enqueue                     {manager, video-id, format}
    tick                        {manager, ms}
    report-failure              {manager, id}
    pick-format                 {formats, policy}
    retry-policy-backoff        {policy, attempt}
    download                    {manager, id}
    active-count                {manager}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: format policy as `where` clause

The v1 modeled `FormatPolicy::{MaxQuality, Lowest, BestUnder(cap)}`
as an ADT. In Innate, the user writes the selection criteria as
prose and the resolver matches:

@format <- @video:formats
    where
        size no more than 500 megabytes
        and resolution at most 1080
    ordered by resolution descending
    first

The `where`-clause form composes: add `and codec is "avc1"` and the
policy refines without needing a new enum variant.

---

## Retry as scheduled state transition

The v1 retry mechanic was a `Retrying { ready_at_ms }` state. In
Innate, the scheduler handles readiness:

on @download-failure
    at @now + [ytd[retry-policy-backoff {policy: @p,
                                           attempt: @attempts}]] ms
    [ytd[retry {id: @id}]]
    where attempts < @p:max-attempts
    || -> #abandoned

`at @future-time @commission` is the native scheduled-trigger form.
The backoff computation and the scheduling are orthogonal.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @formats <- [
        {id: "a", resolution: 480, size-bytes: 50000000, bitrate-bps: 500000}
        {id: "b", resolution: 720, size-bytes: 100000000, bitrate-bps: 1000000}
        {id: "c", resolution: 1080, size-bytes: 200000000, bitrate-bps: 2000000}
    ]

    -> [ytd[pick-format {formats: @formats, policy: {kind: "max-quality"}}]]:id
    ;; -> "c"

    -> [ytd[pick-format {formats: @formats,
                          policy: {kind: "best-under", cap-bytes: 120000000}}]]:id
    ;; -> "b"  (720p fits under 120MB; 1080p at 200MB doesn't)

    -> [ytd[retry-policy-backoff
             {policy: {max-attempts: 3, initial-ms: 1000, multiplier: 2},
              attempt: 2}]]
    ;; -> 2000
]
